          "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001><ENVARGOPEN_0001>Strong effectiveness<ENVARGEND_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a locally Noetherian scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a category fibred in groupoids over <MATH_0003>.\nAssume we have\n<STRUCT_0002>\n<STRUCT_0003> an affine open <MATH_0004>,\n<STRUCT_0004> an inverse system <MATH_0005> of <MATH_0006>-algebras\nwith surjective transition maps whose kernels are locally nilpotent,\n<STRUCT_0005> a system <MATH_0007> of objects of <MATH_0008> lying\nover the system <MATH_0009>.\n<STRUCT_0006>\nIn this situation, set <MATH_0010>. We say that\n<MATH_0011> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>effective<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if there exists an object\n<MATH_0012> of <MATH_0013> over <MATH_0014> whose restriction\nto <MATH_0015> gives the system <MATH_0016>.\n<STRUCT_0007>",
          "source_text_hash": "sha256:f1cfc9190d34076706fab50e865042cb20235cecf20e89da31cf3af8f2ae89d4",
